{"type":"message","id":"acf240f8","parentId":"c825fa8e","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:03:08.926Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-02-17 22:33 GMT+5:30] Perform a root cause analysis of gateway instability and rate limiting issues.\n\nSymptoms:\n- Gateway disconnects without warning\n- Rate limit errors occur, but then reconnection succeeds with the same model\n\nPlease investigate:\n1. Check OpenClaw gateway logs (location? likely in .openclaw-state/logs or similar)\n2. Look for patterns in disconnections, rate limit events, restarts\n3. Analyze configuration that might affect stability (timeouts, keepalives, reconnect settings)\n4. Check if model provider (OpenRouter) is hitting rate limits or intermittent failures\n5. Review gateway and agent settings for resource constraints (memory, file handles)\n6. Identify whether disconnects are from the gateway itself, channel plugins (WhatsApp), or network issues\n7. Provide concrete recommendations to stabilize the system\n\nBe thorough: examine log files, config, and system resources. Return a detailed report with findings and actionable fixes."}],"timestamp":1771347788923}}
{"type":"message","id":"da88dcaf","parentId":"acf240f8","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:03:22.799Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to perform a root cause analysis of gateway instability and rate limiting issues. Let me break down what's needed:\n\n1. Check OpenClaw gateway logs - likely in .openclaw-state/logs or similar\n2. Look for patterns in disconnections, rate limit events, restarts\n3. Analyze configuration affecting stability (timeouts, keepalives, reconnect settings)\n4. Check if OpenRouter is hitting rate limits or intermittent failures\n5. Review gateway and agent settings for resource constraints (memory, file handles)\n6. Identify whether disconnects are from gateway itself, channel plugins (WhatsApp), or network issues\n7. Provide concrete recommendations\n\nI need to be thorough: examine log files, config, and system resources. Return a detailed report with findings and actionable fixes.\n\nLet me start by exploring the workspace structure and finding where the OpenClaw configuration and logs are stored.\n\nFirst, I should check the current directory structure to understand the layout.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll perform a comprehensive root cause analysis of the gateway instability and rate limiting issues. Let me start by exploring the system structure and gathering information."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_58c720d7e9c1455e8a01fb1d","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"pwd","host":"gateway"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":12950,"output":523,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13473,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771347788925}}
