{"type":"message","id":"73ccee55","parentId":"0e6ef814","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:04:22.590Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, the exec command with find isn't returning anything either. This is unusual. Let me try a simpler approach - let me read the AGENTS.md file more thoroughly, specifically sections about the gateway, configuration, and troubleshooting. That might give me insights into common causes of instability and rate limiting.\n\nFrom what I've read so far:\n- Logs are in `/tmp/openclaw/openclaw-YYYY-MM-DD.log`\n- Config is in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`\n- The gateway runs on port 18789 by default\n- The system uses OpenRouter as a model provider\n\nThe symptoms are:\n- Gateway disconnects without warning\n- Rate limit errors occur, but then reconnection succeeds with the same model\n\nThis suggests:\n1. The gateway itself might be restarting or crashing\n2. Network connectivity issues\n3. Resource constraints (memory, file handles)\n4. Rate limiting from the model provider (OpenRouter)\n5. Configuration issues with timeouts, keepalives, reconnect settings\n\nLet me search the codebase for relevant configuration options and code that handles reconnections and rate limiting.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me search the codebase for gateway configuration and rate limiting handling:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f9cf027079e04bef8d7a4ffb","name":"web_search","arguments":{"query":"OpenClaw gateway configuration reconnect timeout keepalive rate limit"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":39639,"output":563,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40202,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771347851864}}
