{"type":"message","id":"1d51da38","parentId":"bf5449de","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:08:11.065Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm seeing a lot of diagnostic logs about lane enqueue/dequeue, agent runs, and many WebSocket closures with code 1008 (policy violation - device identity required). That's expected behavior when the web UI tries to connect without a paired device. Not necessarily a problem.\n\nI still haven't seen explicit \"rate limit\" errors. Let me search for \"429\" or \"rate\" in the log. I can continue reading further down, as the log covers the whole day. Let's jump to a later offset to see if there are any rate limit errors later in the day.\n\nBut maybe the user's issue is not captured in this particular log because the log might be from a different day or the issue occurs sporadically. The date is 2026-02-17. The current date according to the system is 2026-02-17 (from the timestamp in the log). So this is today's log.\n\nThe symptoms: \"Gateway disconnects without warning\" and \"Rate limit errors occur, but then reconnection succeeds with the same model\". I haven't seen any gateway disconnects yet in the log. The gateway started at 03:03:32 and seems to be still running (heartbeat at 05:43). So no disconnect.\n\nMaybe the rate limit errors are coming from the model provider (OpenRouter) when making API calls. Those would show up in logs as errors from the OpenRouter provider. Let me search for \"openrouter\" or \"rate\" or \"429\". Since I can't search directly, I need to scan through more log lines. Let me read a later part, maybe around 3000-4000 lines offset.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me search further in the log for rate limiting or error patterns:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5464a47728ec4f3f94f8be7f","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/tmp/openclaw/openclaw-2026-02-17.log","limit":200,"offset":4000}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","mod