{"type":"message","id":"79c4ead1","parentId":"e76140d5","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:08:27.248Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm still seeing the same pattern: many WebSocket connections from the control UI being closed with code 1008 (policy violation - device identity required). That's normal if no device is paired. The gateway is running fine (heartbeat continues). The WhatsApp channel initially failed to connect (401) but later we saw \"identity changed\" and it might have recovered. I saw at line around 5:39:17 \"identity changed\" which might indicate a reconnection.\n\nI haven't seen any \"rate limit\" errors yet. Let me try to search for \"429\" or \"rate\" by scanning the log more efficiently. Since the log is large, maybe I can use a text search if I could download the file, but I can't. I could read random parts.\n\nMaybe the issue with \"gateway disconnects without warning\" could be related to the gateway process crashing or being killed. In the log, I see the gateway started at 03:03:32 and the heartbeat continues throughout the day. So the gateway hasn't disconnected since the initial start. There were earlier attempts to start gateway when it was already running (port in use). That indicates multiple instances attempted to start, but the main one stayed up.\n\nGiven the symptoms, maybe the user is experiencing disconnections of their channel plugins (like WhatsApp) or model provider rate limiting causing the agent to fail, but the gateway itself remains up. The \"gateway disconnect\" could be a WebSocket connection from a client (like the control UI) getting disconnected, not the gateway server itself.\n\nBut the user said \"Gateway disconnects without warning\" - that could mean the gateway process itself stops or the WebSocket server becomes unreachable. In the log, I see the gateway is stable.\n\nMaybe the log file I'm reading is from a different day or a different machine? The config path in the log shows `C:\\\\Users\\\\mangs\\\\.openclaw\\\\openclaw.json`. That's a different user (mangs) than the one I'm investigating (maybe asus14). But the hostname is ASUS14. That could be the same machine with multiple users. Or maybe the gateway is running under a different user account.\n\nI should check if there are other log files for other days. The log file name is `openclaw-2026-02-17.log`. That's today. There might be logs for other days as well. The issue might occur at times not captured? But the log seems to cover the entire day.\n\nI should search for any \"rate limit\" or \"429\" or \"OpenRouter\" errors. Let me try to search within the log by reading a later offset, maybe around the end of the file, to see if any errors appear later.\n\nBut first, let me calculate the file size: it says 5806 lines total. I've read up to line 4039. There's more. Let me continue reading.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me continue reading the log to find potential rate limit errors:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2415c87fe8544312b5144d68","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/tmp/openclaw/openclaw-2026-02-17.log","limit":200,"offset":5500}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":124658,"output":1358,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":126016,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771348091099}}
